//! C ABI over `rivetkit-core` for foreign-language SDKs. The Java SDK
//! (`rivetkit-java/`) binds it through Java's FFM API with bindings generated by
//! `jextract` from `include/rivetkit.h`.
//!
//! This crate is deliberately thin. Everything an actor host needs (the event
//! loop, hooks, timeouts, streams, the wire protocol, the handle table) lives in
//! `rivetkit-host-adapter`. This crate adds only:
//! - [`abi`]: the exported functions, which convert raw pointers to slices and
//!   call the adapter. It is the only module allowed `unsafe`, and holds exactly
//!   one `unsafe` block.
//! - [`runtime`]: the process-global tokio runtime, the two host callbacks as a
//!   `Transport`, and a log bridge that forwards `tracing` records to the host.

pub mod abi;
mod runtime;

pub use rivetkit_host_adapter::wire::{ABI_VERSION, EventKind, Op, Status};
